Congrats, exciting to see more American open-weight innovation. I tested Inkling-Small last night using the popular Voxel Pagoda prompt learned from @loktar00.

The model ran on 2× RTX 6k GPUs with a 256K context, FP8 KV cache, and 4 max concurrency. After warmup, it generated tokens at around 36 tokens per second, with some variations depending on concurrency. It performs well out of the box and is expected to be tuned further.

@thinkymachines announced Inkling-Small, a model with 276 billion total parameters, of which 12 billion are active. It achieves performance comparable to the larger Inkling model, and the full weights are now available for fine-tuning on Tinker or for use in text, image, and audio interactions on Tinker Playground.

